course: dictionary
lesson: 13074
title: Fewest: the smallest count
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Fewest» tells you the smallest number of things in a group. When you compare groups, the one with the fewest has less than all the others. «Ben made the fewest mistakes in the spelling test» means Ben made less mistakes than everyone else, and no one made fewer.
explain: Use «fewest» only with things you can count, like mistakes, points, coins, or boxes. You cannot count how much water is in a jug, so you would not say the fewest water. Check the sentence: if you can count the things, «fewest» can fit.
explain: In maths, look for the shortest bar on a bar graph or the smallest tally. «Which pet has the fewest votes?» asks you to find the smallest number. «Fewest of all» is a useful phrase when you compare three or more things. Remember that «few» is the basic word, «fewer» compares two things, and «fewest» compares many.
fact: «Fewest» means the smallest number of things.
fact: «Fewest» is the superlative of «few»: few, fewer, fewest.
fact: Use «fewest» for things you can count, such as «the fewest mistakes» or «the fewest points».
fact: «The fewest coins to make 50 cents» is two 25-cent coins.
fact: On a bar graph or tally chart, the fewest is the shortest bar or the smallest count.
exercise: «Mia made the fewest mistakes in the test.» What does fewest mean here? | *The smallest number of mistakes | The largest number of mistakes | The same number as everyone else | Mistakes that are very big
exercise: Cats 9, dogs 4, fish 6. Which pet has the fewest votes? | All three are the same | Fish | *Dogs | Cats
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the smallest number of things. | most | many | biggest | *fewest
